01A4ysknunucyfaTH8kxNmFi","tool_input":{"command":"gh pr create --base main --head bead/spot-p7s --title \"spot-p7s: make the coverage tools fail instead of silently checking nothing\" --body \"## What the bead asked for\n\nTwo coverage tools whose stated scope and actual scope differed:\n\n1. \\`scripts/check_claims.py\\` excluded missing artifacts from its exit condition, so \\`make clean && make lint-all\\` (clean deletes every \\`artifacts/*.json\\`) reported green while verifying nothing.\n2. The root Makefile guarded each app with \\`if [ -x \\$a/.venv/bin/ruff ]\\`, so an app with no venv was silently skipped and lint-all exited 0.\n3. \\`cadence\\`'s lint target covered \\`src tests\\` where the other four apps cover \\`src tests scripts\\`, and \\`cadence/scripts\\` had two files \\`ruff format\\` would rewrite while \\`make -C cadence lint\\` exited 0.\n\n## What I did\n\n- \\`check_claims.py\\`: a missing registered artifact is now a failure (\\`MISSING\\`, deduped to one line per artifact) included in the exit condition. The success line reads \\`all 18 claims match\\` since a partial count is no longer reachable.\n- Root \\`Makefile\\`: the per-app loop now exits 1 naming the missing \\`\\$a/.venv/bin/ruff\\` and the exact remedy CI uses (\\`uv sync --extra dev --project \\$a\\`), instead of skipping.\n- \\`cadence/Makefile\\`: lint covers \\`src tests scripts\\`; the two drifted files (\\`build_demo.py\\`, \\`insert_demo.py\\`) are formatted. No behavior change in either script.\n\n## How the acceptance criteria were met\n\n- *check_claims.py exits non-zero when any registered artifact is missing* — verified: hiding \\`ostinato/artifacts/sim_report.json\\` → exit 1 with a MISSING section; restored → exit 0, 18/18.\n- *lint-all exits non-zero when any app in APPS lacks a venv* — verified: removing gamut's ruff → exit 2 with the named path and remedy; full venvs → whole gate green (lint-all plus all five test suites run locally).\n- *cadence lint covers src tests scripts, two unformatted files fixed* — verified: \\`make -C cadence lint\\` green including scripts.\n\n## Self-review (ADR 0013)\n\nThree lenses, seven findings recorded in \\`.flywheel/review.jsonl\\`: five accepted (comment/counter mismatch flagged by two lenses, guard message misdiagnosis, remedy ordering, X/X ratio, rationale moved to a comment), two rejected with reasons (deleting the guard outright; dropping the uv sync hint).\n\n## Deliberately left out\n\n- No new drift hunting — this makes existing checks honest about their own scope, per the bead's ESTABLISHES/DOES NOT.\n- Note for the reviewer: this branch was rebuilt onto \\`main\\` because its original base was \\`bead/spot-2ig\\`, whose PR #4 merged into \\`fleet/builder-permissions\\` at 11:59Z — *after* that branch's own PR #3 merged to main at 11:44Z. spot-2ig's commits are therefore currently stranded off \\`main\\` (the exact child-PR trap ADR 0009 warns about) and are deliberately not bundled here.\n\nCloses spot-p7s.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\"","description":"Open PR for spot-p7s"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":3},"started_in_background":3,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":57,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Bead spot-p7s → PR #7 opened: https://github.com/jamesponwith/spotify-recsys-ecosystem/pull/7**\n\n**What I did.** All three fixes from the bead: `check_claims.py` now exits 1 when any registered artifact is missing (deduped to one MISSING line per artifact), root `lint-all` exits 1 naming the missing `.venv/bin/ruff` and the CI-canonical `uv sync` remedy instead of silently skipping the app, and cadence's lint target now covers `src tests scripts` with its two drifted files (`build_demo.py`, `insert_demo.py`) formatted.\n\n**Gate: green.** Both reproducers verified before and after (hidden artifact → exit 1; removed ruff → lint-all exit 2 with the named path), full `make lint-all` and all five app test suites pass locally. I built all five venvs in the worktree to run it — a previous builder abandoned a bead for lack of them, but `uv` was reachable.\n\n**Self-review (ADR 0013).** Three lenses, seven findings in the ledger: five accepted (the strongest — two lenses independently caught my dedup comment contradicting the problem counter; correctness caught the guard message misdiagnosing \"no venv\" when only ruff is missing), two rejected with reasons recorded. Fixes applied before the PR.\n\n**One complication worth your attention.** This worktree was cut from `bead/spot-2ig`, and spot-2ig's PR #4 merged into `fleet/builder-permissions` *fifteen minutes after* that branch's own PR #3 merged to main — the exact child-PR trap ADR 0009 warns about. spot-2ig's three commits are currently stranded off main. I rebuilt my branch commit-by-commit onto `origin/main` so PR #7 stays one revertible idea (and caught spot-2ig's `audit-lexicon` target trying to ride along), and filed **spot-ln4 (P1)** for the human decision on how to land the stranded work.\n\nBead spot-p7s stays open until PR #7 merges (labeled w:2), reservations released, worktree left for the spawner to clean up. Cost: ~75k subagent tokens for the review panel plus this session.","ttft_ms":14327,"type":"result","duration_ms":377687,"uuid":"74aec0fa-cfd8-4d0f-a4aa-1f08af898032","ttft_stream_ms":1789,"time_to_request_ms":21,"queued_turn_count":0}
